  [38;5;153mtest/prefs.test.js[39m using [38;5;153mnode:test[39m + [38;5;153mnode:assert[39m, with a hand-rolled fake storage object and a throwing variant. [38;5;153mnpm [39m
  [38;5;153mtest[39m runs [38;5;153mnode --test[39m. Cases: round-trip; missing key returns the fallback; [38;5;153mremove[39m; [38;5;153mclear[39m; unrelated keys survive a
  write; corrupt JSON degrades to the fallback; a throwing storage never propagates and behaves in-memory.

  [1mStated plainly:[0m the [38;5;153mapp.js[39m DOM wiring is [3mnot[0m covered by these tests — that was the trade in choosing zero-dependency
  over jsdom. I'd verify the checkbox behavior by loading [38;5;153mindex.html[39m in a browser and reloading, and I'll report that as
  a manual check, not an automated one.

  [1mThe one open choice[0m

  How [38;5;153mprefs.js[39m gets loaded by both the browser and the test runner:

  - [1mES module[0m — [38;5;153mindex.html[39m becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m, and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m does [38;5;153mimport { createPrefs } from [39m
    [38;5;153m'./prefs.js'[39m. Clean, standard, no shims. Costs: changes how [38;5;153mapp.js[39m loads (module scripts are deferred and scoped, so
    the existing top-level [38;5;153mgetElementById[39m still works, but the file is no longer a classic script), and [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m
    needs [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m — [1mwhich would break [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m, since it uses [38;5;153mrequire[0m. Workaround is naming the tests [38;5;153m.mjs[39m
    or leaving [38;5;153msrc/[39m as [38;5;153m.cjs[39m. That collateral edit to [38;5;153msrc/[39m is the part I don't love.
  - [1mClassic script with a dual-export tail[0m — [38;5;153mprefs.js[39m defines a global and appends [38;5;153mif (typeof module !== 'undefined') [39m
    [38;5;153mmodule.exports = ...[39m. Matches the repo's current plain-script style exactly, touches nothing in [38;5;153msrc/[39m, no
    [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m change. Costs: that trailing conditional is a mild wart.

  [1mMy recommendation: the classic script.[0m The wart is three lines and self-explanatory; the ESM route drags an unrelated,
  working Node file into a task that has nothing to do with it, which is the kind of collateral change I'd rather not
  make without you asking for it.
